  <subsection xml:id="subsec-132-LearningTargets">
    <title>Learning Targets (LTs)</title>

    <p>
      Here is a list of the 22 LTs for this course. Most will only be referred to by number 
      (as in, "This week's quiz will cover LTs #12, 13 and 14.") so you will need to refer to this list frequently.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>
        <p>
          Use bar diagrams and units to solve measurement word problems.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Convert between units of length, weight, and capacity, and solve arithmetic problems.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Define, identify, and provide examples of different types of angles and related terminology, and solve problems involving angles.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Define, identify, and use concepts related to angles, parallel/perpendicular lines, triangles, and circles, and use these to solve problems and answer questions.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve problems using the interior angle sum and exterior angles of a triangle.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Identify, provide examples of, and answer questions about different types of triangles and quadrilaterals.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Write a clear "Teacher's Solution" for an unknown angle problem.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Identify types of angles relating to parallel lines, and use parallel lines, transversals, and auxiliary lines to solve unknown angle problems.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Apply the sum of interior and exterior angles of polygons to solve problems.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Determine whether two triangles are congruent, and use congruent triangles to solve problems.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve problems involving area, including composite figures and regions with holes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Justify and apply formulas for the area of triangles, parallelograms, and trapezoids.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve problems using the Pythagorean Theorem and its converse, both with and without square roots.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve problems involving similarity and scaling, including applications to right triangles.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Determine whether two triangles are similar, and use similar triangles to solve problems.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Convert between units of area and explain how scaling affects area.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve problems involving pi and the circumference of circles.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve problems involving the area of a circle.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Answer questions and solve problems about units of volume, and calculate basic volumes.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Solve problems using the volumes of cylinders, cones, pyramids, and spheres.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Calculate the mean, median, and mode of a data set, and solve related problems.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <p>
          Develop a probability model for an experiment and its sample space, and use it to determine probabilities of events.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
    
  </subsection>
</section>
